Z||000008||Songman||08-23-2001||08:18 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>Odds on this one are like being struck by lightning while being attacked by a shark.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Have you heard about all of the shark attacks lately?!? More than a dozen in the last few weeks! I'm feeling lucky! Thunderstorms are heading into Nashville too! Guess I'll be riding back to KY for some tickets. Made the trip on Wednesday and spent $10. Another $10 tomorrow! Chances on Wednesday were 1 in 80 million. Wonder what it will be this time.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>I only caught the tail end of the news last night on the truck radio (out spraying the lawn for weeds).  Somebody spent over $600.00 on tickets   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> (others only the typical buck or two) and this person couldn't even afford grocieries!  Go figure!<P>Now that is just darn right silly.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One guy at the place I go in Franklin, KY bought $2000 worth of tickets! I wonder if he'll try again...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||08-23-2001||08:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>  <BR>Chances on Wednesday were 1 in 80 million.  Wonder what it will be this time.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The odds don't change.  The odds of winning the jackpot, whether it is $10 million or $300 million, are always 1 in 80 million (since there are 80 million different number combinations).<P>The difference now is that since the jackpot is so high many more tickets are being sold.  This means the odds are good that someone will win the jackpot on Saturday.<P>For Wednesdays drawing, approximately 77% of the 80 million number combinations were taken......they are guessing that over 90% will be taken up for Saturdays drawing.  <P>That means there is a 90% probability that someone will win on Saturday......if no one does, the jackpot will be well over $400 million for next week!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||JSocha||08-23-2001||10:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>  One guy at the place I go in Franklin, KY bought $2000 worth of tickets! I wonder if he'll try again...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry dear, its all gone.  I spent our vacation money I have been saving up for the past 20 years on power ball tickets.<P>What does that mean?<P>Well dear, it means we won't be going to the Super 8 motel for our vacation down the block like I promised again this year.||||reg||10
Z||000011||8Ball||08-24-2001||12:22 AM||||If I win (wishful thinking)<P>I am buying an 88 gt t-tops and dropping it off at archies for a chop top and a 700 hp v8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> enuf money can do anything  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> will 50 grand cover it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Pontiaddict||08-24-2001||03:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B> <BR>The odds don't change.  The odds of winning the jackpot, whether it is $10 million or $300 million, are always 1 in 80 million (since there are 80 million different number combinations).<P>The difference now is that since the jackpot is so high many more tickets are being sold.  This means the odds are good that someone will win the jackpot on Saturday.<P>For Wednesdays drawing, approximately 77% of the 80 million number combinations were taken......they are guessing that over 90% will be taken up for Saturdays drawing.  <P>That means there is a 90% probability that someone will win on Saturday......if no one does, the jackpot will be well over $400 million for next week!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are you sure those numbers are right?<BR>That would be a great invenstment for some company, spend $80 million to get all the combinations of numbers and win $400 million.<P>The lottery in MI has odds of something like 1:400 billion. I can't remember back far enough to High school math class when we had to figure that out.||||reg||1
Z||000013||mrfiero||08-24-2001||03:26 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B> Are you sure those numbers are right?<BR>That would be a great invenstment for some company, spend $80 million to get all the combinations of numbers and win $400 million.</B><P><BR>The problem with that is you run the risk of multiple winners.  If someone bought 80 million tickets on top of the rest of the country (another 60-70 million tickets) the odds of only one winning ticket are astronomical.  There would likely be 2, maybe 3 winning tickets, so your $80 million investment wouldn't reap much.  You'd be hard pressed to get 80 million tickets printed up in time anyways.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR><B>The lottery in MI has odds of something like 1:400 billion. I can't remember back far enough to High school math class when we had to figure that out.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That's not right.  If the odds were that high no one would ever win your jackpots!  The regular Colorado lotto has odds of 1 in 5.2 million......our jackpots rarely get higher than 5 or 6 million though ($27 million is the record).<P><BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.powerball.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.powerball.com</A>   for more info.  The odds of winning the big jackpot <BR>are actually 1 in 80,089,128.<P>||||reg||1
