Z||000019||Cheever3000||08-25-2001||07:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR> spend $80 million to get all the combinations of numbers and win $400 million.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Another problem with this is filling out all those cards (assuming Powerball is like the other lotteries I've seen).<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||mrfiero||08-25-2001||11:26 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B> [QUOTE] spend $80 million to get all the combinations of numbers and win $400 million.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Another problem with this is filling out all those cards (assuming Powerball is like the other lotteries I've seen).<P></B>[/QUOTE]<P><BR>There's the "quick pick" option.  The computer will pick the number for you, but you're right......to insure you get all 80+ million combinations with no duplicates you'd have to fill out those little cards.<P>There still wouldn't be enough time to print them all out though.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
